    "By confining all administrative chores to Friday afternoon, you protect the high-energy days of Monday through Thursday for pure commercial expansion. Friday afternoon is naturally a lower-energy window where client meetings are rare and deep creative focus is winding down. Executing administrative tasks while listening to ambient music on Friday cleans your operational slate, leaving you with zero nagging chores over the weekend.",
    "Automate your administrative workflows wherever possible. Use scheduling links (such as Calendly or Cal.com) with strict availability buffers to eliminate the exhausting back-and-forth email dance of scheduling meetings. Use Make.com to automatically route client invoices to your accounting software and log receipts in cloud folders without human intervention.",
